WEBVTT

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.010
"This is a work of fiction based on research
into the period in which it is set. The people,
organization, laws, and names that appear in it
have no relation to any in the real world."

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.030
"The Last Blue Sky"

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.070
Let me see.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.990
The Imperial Hotel article
by the end of construction,

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:03.080
the human combustion and
Yoshiwara poisoning articles, and...

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.580
Oh, the motion picture with Defrott!

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.960
I've got to hurry!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.800
The sky is... red.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.010
What?

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.340
Excuse me...

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.030
Wha...

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.690
What's going on?

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.870
Huh?

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.700
What?

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.490
I feel like we're going around in circles.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.950
What?!

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.250
Didn't Takeuchi give you directions?

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:55.630
Yes, but I get kind of lost because
of this smell and the echoes.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.970
I guess we should go outside
and check where we are.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.430
We'll burn to death if we go outside.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.510
The sun should be up by now.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.140
Let's go. I think it's this way.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:11.230
I wish Takeuchi had thought
of a better way for us to go.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.320
Still, we're lucky that
this sewer connects to HQ.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.110
I wanted to chase after them, too.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.700
The vampire units?

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:20.990
Yeah.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:28.540
They moved with perfect coordination.
That takes discipline.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.040
Aren't you curious where they came from?

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.460
That's true, but who do you
think was leading them?

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.500
What do you mean?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:40.340
We work as a unit because we have Maeda, right?

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.550
But they didn't seem
to have a commanding officer.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:49.220
If that's true, it means
they've had serious training.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.480
Vampire units,

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.740
you are my pride and joy.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.580
I knew Lieutenant General Nakajima
was up to something.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.090
Where did these guys come from?

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.960
I don't know.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.630
Counting their beds,
it looks like there're about 80.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.680
I'm impressed.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.770
They even have name tags.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.730
No cut corners.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.900
Looks like there are still vacancies.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.820
I would look closer at him.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.740
--I must look at him closer.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.030
--I must look at him closer.
--Where is her voice coming from?

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.160
--I am Salomé, daughter of Herodias,
Princess of Judea.
--Where is her voice coming from?

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.200
--I am Salomé, daughter of Herodias,
Princess of Judea.
--The recording?

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.040
--I am Salomé, daughter of Herodias,
Princess of Judea.
--It's running.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.500
Speak again, Jokanaan.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.340
Yes, a fine Salomé.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.920
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.300
What did you think of the script I wrote?

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.680
A touring threepenny play.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.680
The damage extended to civilians.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.270
Every undertaking requires sacrifices.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:22.530
But you need a trumpeter to make
your toy soldiers march, don't you?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:27.490
I hope it doesn't become the trumpet
that signals the end of the world.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.990
Revelation. You're well-educated.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:35.790
I'm facing all of you.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.420
I've looked into a lot of things.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.710
"A-class vampire
Misaki Nakajima
Recording No. 6"

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.760
Now,

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.630
use this place as you see fit.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.680
It's sunless, even in daytime.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.180
Have no fear.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:59.100
What was in here that could destroy
the place so thoroughly?

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.570
Still, as a starting point,

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:05.320
it's not bad.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.370
Let's see, this is the Imperial Hotel,
that's human combustion,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.620
that's Yoshiwara, and these are...

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.500
Boss.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.580
What?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.290
What's this manuscript?

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.670
It's about Yokohama. I'm about to head there.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.800
Yokohama?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.970
There was a riot near the Red Brick Warehouse.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:30.640
I hear it turned serious
and the army put it down.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.850
Wow, I had no idea.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.350
Rumor has it people were attacked
by vampires or something.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.680
Vampires?!

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.810
It's just--

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.600
What are you doing?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.940
I'm going with you!

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.650
It's just a load of nonsense!

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.530
There's no such thing as vampires.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:49.240
Besides, don't you have work to do?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.580
Get that Imperial Hotel article ready
by the end of construction.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:54.740
Fine.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.750
"Tenmanya"

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.040
--Ow, ow, ow.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.340
--What's wrong, Santaro?
--Ow, ow, ow.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.420
Oh, Shinnosuke.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.590
It's those damn rats.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:10.840
Rats?

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.930
I don't see any.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.310
Good grief.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:20.890
The day dawns blood red, then ends
with a grand procession of rats.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:25.440
All today's good for is
drinking and going to bed.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.780
The sun is still up, you know.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:32.110
The sun can't get into my house.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.070
There we go!

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.030
Well, pardon me.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.920
It looks like it will be another hot day.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.220
We're finally back to
someplace that smells decent.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.600
So, this is where it comes out.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.470
Huh?

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.720
What's wrong?

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.560
Doesn't it feel different from usual, somehow?

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.230
How so? Nothing's changed.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.280
It's like I can't hear enough noises.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.650
--Noises?
--Yes.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:17.990
There should be a mix of footsteps
and people talking and things.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:20.290
Well, I'm just an unranked.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:23.250
I can't hear everything you can.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.630
S-Sorry.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.670
Forget it.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.090
Let's go up.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:29.090
Right!

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.520
Let me see...

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:47.650
Once the Imperial Hotel's done,
there's human combustion, Yoshiwara, and...

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.650
Huh? What's the other one?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.400
Man, it sure is hot for September.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.950
Don't talk about it;
it makes it feel even hotter.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:59.410
I can't help how hot it is.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:00.870
Anyway, look.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.040
What is this?

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.170
Vampires!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.040
Huh?!

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.500
The truth behind the Yokohama riot!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.510
Everyone bitten turned
into a vampire and rioted!

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:14.340
What?!

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.680
You said there was an incident
in Yoshiwara, right?

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.220
Yes! Vampires must be behind
human combustion, too!

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.180
All right!

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.190
From now on, we'll be the vampire newspaper!

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.270
Yes!

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.610
First, hand me that.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.980
What?

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.530
The vampire.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.780
Dragon fruit. You know, dragon fruit.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.860
Do you mean...

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.830
<i>Dracula?</i>

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.340
Maeda, are you well already?

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.010
Well enough.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.390
Thank goodness. What a relief.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.600
It is not. Shouldn't you get more rest?

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.270
You have heart trouble.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:06.560
It's my body. It's none of your business.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.900
And the Yokohama operation?
Were there S-classes?

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:15.900
Yes, but by the time we infiltrated,
all the S-classes were already dead, and...

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.740
Who killed them?

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:18.990
We don't know.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:22.950
Are you telling me you returned
without finding out?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.370
We're sorry.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.290
We didn't get the chance.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:32.790
A mob of hostile vampires appeared
and tried to attack the townspeople.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.920
And you subdued them alone?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.180
No, the vampire units came and...

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.720
Who was leading them?

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.850
I couldn't spot their leader.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.390
And Ltg. Nakajima?

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:47.230
We came back here to find that out.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.230
Oh.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.270
What?

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:53.150
I hear a Model T engine.
It's probably Ltg. Nakajima.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:02.450
He's inside.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.500
How are you feeling, Maeda?

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.500
I'm well enough.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:18.470
I see. In that case, return to the scene.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:21.510
Everyone is waiting for you.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:26.970
Ltg. Nakajima, I have a question.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.600
What is it, Yamagami?

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.440
That group we saw in Yokohama...

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.480
Who are they?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.860
They're vampire units.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:41.280
Have they been perfected?

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:44.370
There's still room for research.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.620
However,

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:49.910
they are shaping up into the force I envisioned.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:54.330
Who are they?

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:58.800
They are vampire units. That's all.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.630
No, I mean, where did those vampires come from?

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.930
Kurusu, that's rude.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:08.680
I don't mind, Yamagami. He's young.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.230
And also

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.560
a vampire.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:16.060
Common sense hardly applies to him.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.110
Kurusu.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.480
Sir.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.990
How much do you know about vampire units?

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.910
They use vampire powers
in a special forces unit.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:31.370
Their main duty is to discover
and secure or dispose of vamps.

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:34.330
Yes, exactly.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:40.960
Have you heard that a military intelligence
unit like Britain's vampire forces

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:45.050
was the original objective
of the vampire unit plan?

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:45.890
Yes, sir.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:50.220
And why I wanted to establish this unit?

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.680
Well...

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:57.810
You see, I never wanted to lose
a man on the battlefield again.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:02.280
So, I concluded that,
in order for no soldier to die,

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:07.240
they would need to possess immortal bodies.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:11.950
Time moves quickly in the world.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:19.170
The vampire unit plan must be constantly
evolving just as quickly to keep up.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:23.920
Finding and recruiting vampires
off the streets as we have done

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.720
is already an outdated method
of increasing our ranks.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:34.640
So, I changed tack and decided to focus
on efficiently manufacturing vampires.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.560
"Manufacturing"?

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.610
Lieutenant General!
What exactly do you mean by that?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:42.610
I mean that I literally
succeeded in creating vampires.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.700
Using Ascra.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.780
Our research encountered this,

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:56.210
and Ascra, which can turn humans into
vampires almost perfectly, was completed.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.750
This is truly the fruit of wisdom.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:06.380
And by using this on my highly
capable men, I create vampire units.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:09.680
Then the vampire units in Yokohama are...

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:14.350
You turned all the members of
Special Forces Unit 16 into vampires?!

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.480
I merely

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:22.940
gave them virtual immortality.

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.320
Maeda,

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.610
you're the only one left.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.240
Maeda, stop!

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:39.120
My life has been Ltg. Nakajima's
since he saved it on that battlefield.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.340
That's what I live for.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.630
Thank you, Maeda.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:50.930
Once you become a vampire unit,
my ideal force will be complete.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:53.010
There's just one thing.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.970
What is it?

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:59.020
Misaki... asked me to stop you.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.610
Oh?

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:06.900
It was written in a letter she left me
while becoming a vampire.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.910
I'm amazed she regained
consciousness in that state.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.490
Truly regrettable.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:17.410
She was my daughter,
but she was always distant, somehow.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:23.500
You two were supposed to marry
and support me together one day, but...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.510
Still, Maeda,

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.420
you're different, aren't you?

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:34.510
You know how much passion
I've poured into the vampire unit plan.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:40.640
Drink that Ascra dry for me.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.230
Maeda!

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:45.440
What do you want to become a vampire for?

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:48.650
You'll be like us--no food or drink but blood!

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:56.580
Ltg. Nakajima! This is inhuman!

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.950
Don't talk about humanity, vampire!

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:08.550
It certainly is comical to hear that
from a nonhuman like him.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:11.260
Lieutenant General, that's despicable.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.510
You're probably right.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:19.310
But if I hadn't made my choice,
Japan would continue down the wrong path.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:22.730
It would become a worthless country

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:29.780
where vapid old men line their pockets,
supported by the sacrifice of young lives.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:31.740
How was it in Siberia?

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.200
Wasn't it only young soldiers who died?

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.910
"That expedition was a mistake."

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.410
With those words,

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:44.330
the people in power dismissed
all the young men who were sacrificed.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:48.340
I want to do something about this country.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:55.090
I want to make a world where young people
can smile and speak of the future.

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:59.060
That doesn't justify sacrificing
our comrades in arms!

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.930
They didn't become sacrifices.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.350
They became heroes.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.860
This won't do.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:11.740
It's time for lunch with
the new chief secretary.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.900
Maeda, I leave the rest to you.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:17.030
They're your men.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.410
Nakajima!

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.010
Yamagami!

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:38.220
Move, and I'll kill you, too!

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.270
Maeda...

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.530
Our future generals,

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:00.830
I salute you!

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:15.010
Maeda, let's stop this.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:17.470
We're comrades, aren't we?

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:19.510
Quiet, vampire!

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:22.890
Listen, Maeda.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:26.810
When did you get like this?

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.900
I haven't changed.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:34.070
It's the lieutenant general who
wants to sell reality for his ideals.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:38.780
He stole the futures of all those
young special forces soldiers.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:46.160
While we struggle desperately to stay human,

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:51.130
how can you all sacrifice
your humanity so easily?

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:00.720
Kurusu!

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.510
Maeda, run!

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:15.940
Maeda?

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.530
Yamagami? So, you're all right.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.950
Yeah. That was a big earthquake.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.910
If I weren't a vampire, I'd be dead. You?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.250
I don't know. It's so dark.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.710
You're behind this debris?

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.540
I'll get you out soon.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.130
Don't collapse it.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:36.050
Oh, you're alive.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:39.090
As if I'd let that kill me.

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:40.380
Got a light?

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.010
My arm won't move.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.010
Hang on.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.940
That hits the spot.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.320
I'll get you out now, okay?

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:05.330
--Yamagami.
--What?

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:07.700
Let's go for a drink, just us.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.910
Where did that come from?

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:14.290
Then again, you were always
a tempura man, weren't you?

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.420
Can't eat it now, though.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:23.340
There's one thing I want to apologize for.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.760
What?

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:31.730
When we were at Ichigaya,
someone stole your belt once, remember?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:35.730
Yeah. I got a real beating
from my superior officer.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.480
I'm the one who stole it.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:39.440
That was you?!

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:43.910
You were an intellectual, but you could be slow.

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.660
Nothing good comes of being with you, huh?

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:50.540
You got that right.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:05.760
Yamagami!

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:10.720
If I weren't a vampire, I'd be a pancake.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.480
Yamagami.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.350
Just this one left.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:16.730
Hey.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:22.190
It looks hot outside.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.490
There it goes.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:26.450
Idiot! Stop it!

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:30.120
Listen, Maeda, take good care of Kurusu.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.580
He's a good kid.

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:32.960
Yamagami, stop!

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:35.750
Also, about that belt.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:38.590
I'm the one who stole it first.

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:40.340
Stop!

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:44.220
I could really go for some tempura.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:11.950
"September 1, Taisho 12 (1923),
at 32 seconds past 11:58 A.M.,
an earthquake rocked Tokyo."

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:46.920
"The Letter"
